[E-TAILREC] Error: `count` is marked @[tailrec], but a recursive call isn't in tail position
   ╭─[ reject/tailrec-let.sw:9:14 ]
   │
 9 │     let r := count xs
   │              ────┬───  
   │                  ╰───── its result is bound to `r`, and the block goes on after it
   │ 
   │ Note 1: a call is in tail position when its result is the function's result, with nothing left to do after it returns; then each call is a turn of a loop, not a new frame
   │ 
   │ Note 2: to use the result, carry it along in an extra parameter (an accumulator) that the call updates
───╯
